<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Thanks Colin,<br>I suspect that if someone buys a brand new one from a high volume seller they would be best to try V5 firmware first regardless of what it says on the PCB or the original CPS read of the radio.<br>Most likely that people are getting the latest version if its from a high volume seller.</div></blockquote>Probably all radios bought new now will be what we call V5.<br><br>Its strange however that your PCB has V2.1 written on it, because my two MD9600 which are over a year old have V4A written on the PCB, and since there are also radios with V4 written on the PCB, we call the V4A radios V5.<br><br>I'm pretty sure someone posted here saying their PCB acually had V5 written on it.<br><br>So its quite bizarre your V5 board has V2 written on it.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Sep 21, 2024 10:21 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
