		<published>2024-09-20T18:59:48</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33096#p33096</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33096#p33096"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD9600 no RX/TX]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33096#p33096"><![CDATA[
That's good news. The markings on the board can't really be relied upon. Our definition of V2, V4 , V5 is only something we invented for our own use. The manufacturers don't seem to identify the different versions. <br><br> The differences are in the synthesiser chips and the IF chips, so only the correct version will work. <br><br>If the radio receives and transmits then you must be using the correct version.<br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Fri Sep 20, 2024 6:59 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
