		<author><name><![CDATA[GM4SVM]]></name></author>
		<updated>2024-09-20T13:32:06</updated>

		<published>2024-09-20T13:32:06</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33095#p33095</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33095#p33095"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD9600 no RX/TX]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33095#p33095"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Same issue here Colin, but its a recent radio. Definitely says that version.<br><br>I tested the radio on original firmware and it was sending and receiving on FM.<br>I did that just to check the hardware and then I ran a backup of the original system.<br><br>Tested on FM it goes into transmit but no RF out.<br>On receive it receives nothing - not even from a handheld in the same room.<br>Its clearly a firmware version.<br><br>I think what's happened here is there are V4 or V5 radios in the wild with V2.1 screen printed on the board!<br>Mine had the GPS sticker on it but no GPS as someone else had mentioned. Although mine wasn't sold as GPS anyway.<br>Same number sticker on the side too.<br><br>I am going to flash the V5 firmware to it and see if that works.<br>If it doesn't I will try V4.<br><br>Probably not today as I am a bit tired, but its one of the challenges doing this type of thing!<br><br>73.</div></blockquote>Hi Colin.<br>I decided to give it a go after I had my lunch.<br>V5 firmware worked.<br>Full TX/RX. DMR and FM working perfectly.<br><br>So we do have radios out there with V2 printed on the board that wont work on V2 firmware.<br><br>Open GD77 is a great enhancement of these radios.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1560">GM4SVM</a> — Fri Sep 20, 2024 1:32 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
		<entry>
		<author><name><![CDATA[GM4SVM]]></name></author>
		<updated>2024-09-20T11:52:29</updated>

		<published>2024-09-20T11:52:29</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33092#p33092</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33092#p33092"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: MD9600 no RX/TX]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4065&amp;p=33092#p33092"><![CDATA[
Same issue here Colin, but its a recent radio. Definitely says that version.<br><br>I tested the radio on original firmware and it was sending and receiving on FM.<br>I did that just to check the hardware and then I ran a backup of the original system.<br><br>Tested on FM it goes into transmit but no RF out.<br>On receive it receives nothing - not even from a handheld in the same room.<br>Its clearly a firmware version.<br><br>I think what's happened here is there are V4 or V5 radios in the wild with V2.1 screen printed on the board!<br>Mine had the GPS sticker on it but no GPS as someone else had mentioned. Although mine wasn't sold as GPS anyway.<br>Same number sticker on the side too.<br><br>I am going to flash the V5 firmware to it and see if that works.<br>If it doesn't I will try V4.<br><br>Probably not today as I am a bit tired, but its one of the challenges doing this type of thing!<br><br>73.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1560">GM4SVM</a> — Fri Sep 20, 2024 11:52 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
